    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🤖 Between Step 1 and Step 2 — Claude does this, not n8n\n\n`Needs edit` rows aren't picked up automatically. **You ping Claude** to process them: it generates a soundtrack (vidiq_generate_music) and assembles the cut (vidiq_compose — clip + music + a title overlay, rendered to MP4), then reads/writes the row directly through a Google Drive + Sheets connector, setting status to `Ready to schedule`. No n8n node calls vidIQ — its tools only exist through Claude's own chat connection — and this runs on request, not on a schedule.",
        "width": 590,
        "height": 260,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "sticky-0-610",
      "name": "Note 0-610",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        610
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🗺️ How to read this canvas\n\nThree numbered n8n steps, left to right, plus one step that ISN'T n8n (see the note below Step 1). Inside each step, colour tells you what a box does: 🟩 green = something a person gives it or approves · 🟦 blue = finding/deciding what's due · 🟪 purple = automated work · 🟥 red = the irreversible action (writing, publishing) · 🟨 yellow = a safety branch.\n\nSteps are separate n8n triggers under the hood (a Drive watch, two schedules, a Telegram webhook) — they hand off to each other only through the **status** column of the shared \"Content Calendar\" Google Sheet, never through a wire on the canvas.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 320,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky--400--360",
      "name": "Note -400--360",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -400,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🚦 Do this first — nothing runs without these\n\n**1. Google Drive** — folders `Raw Uploads` and `Edited`; copy each ID from its URL into the matching `REPLACE_WITH_..._FOLDER_ID` field.\n\n**2. Google Sheet** `Content Calendar` with headers: `date_added pillar format raw_file_link edited_file_link title description tags thumbnail_link scheduled_datetime status telegram_message_id youtube_url`. Copy its ID into every `REPLACE_WITH_SHEET_ID`.\n\n**3. n8n credentials** — one Google OAuth2 (Drive+Sheets scopes), one Telegram bot (via @BotFather) plus your chat id (via @userinfobot).\n\n**4. YouTube Data API v3** — Google Cloud Console → new project → enable the API → OAuth consent screen → OAuth client → connect it as a YouTube credential in n8n, signed in as the channel's own account. See Step 3's note for the full sequence.\n\n**5. Claude's own Google connector** — see the note below Step 1. vidIQ needs no separate setup; it's already connected.",
        "width": 700,
        "height": 340,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky-260--380",
      "name": "Note 260--380",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        260,
        -380
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyMinute"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggerOn": "specificFolder",
        "folderToWatch": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "REPLACE_WITH_RAW_UPLOADS_FOLDER_ID"
        },
        "event": "fileCreated"
      },
      "id": "g1trig",
      "name": "New file in Raw Uploads",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleDriveTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        80,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "Fires when a new video or photo lands in the 'Raw Uploads' Drive folder. Replace the folder ID with your own once the folder exists.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "name": "pillar",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.name.split('_')[0] }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "format",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.mimeType.includes('video') ? ($json.name.toLowerCase().includes('short') ? 'short' : 'long') : 'photo' }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "raw_file_link",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.webViewLink }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "set1",
      "name": "Guess pillar & format from filename",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        300,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "Cheap first guess only — assumes files are named like 'pillarname_2026-09-08_topic.mp4'. Rename the row's pillar/format by hand in the Sheet if the guess is wrong.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "append",
        "documentId": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "REPLACE_WITH_SHEET_ID"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "Content Calendar"
        },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "value": {
            "date_added": "={{ $now.toISODate() }}",
            "pillar": "={{ $json.pillar }}",
            "format": "={{ $json.format }}",
            "raw_file_link": "={{ $json.raw_file_link }}",
            "status": "Needs edit"
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "append1",
      "name": "Log into Content Calendar",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        80,
        430
      ],
      "notes": "One new row per raw file, status 'Needs edit'. From here it's picked up by Claude (you ping to trigger it — see the sheet note) rather than by another n8n workflow.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 9 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "cron2",
      "name": "Every day 9am",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        840,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "Runs once a day. Change the cron expression for a different review time.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "readRows",
        "documentId": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "REPLACE_WITH_SHEET_ID"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "Content Calendar"
        },
        "filtersUI": {
          "values": [
            {
              "lookupColumn": "status",
              "lookupValue": "Scheduled"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "read2",
      "name": "Find items due for review",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1060,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "Rows you moved to 'Scheduled' in the Sheet — Claude-edited, then titled and dated by you, just not yet approved.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "chatId": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID",
        "text": "=🎬 *{{ $json.title }}*\\nPillar: {{ $json.pillar }} · Format: {{ $json.format }}\\nScheduled: {{ $json.scheduled_datetime }}\\n\\n{{ $json.edited_file_link }}",
        "additionalFields": {
          "parse_mode": "Markdown"
        },
        "replyMarkup": "inlineKeyboard",
        "inlineKeyboard": {
          "rows": [
            {
              "row": {
                "buttons": [
                  {
                    "text": "✅ Approve",
                    "additionalFields": {
                      "callback_data": "=approve|{{ $json.row_number }}"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "❌ Reject",
                    "additionalFields": {
                      "callback_data": "=reject|{{ $json.row_number }}"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "tg2",
      "name": "Send approval request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        840,
        430
      ],
      "notes": "The confirm-before-publish gate from Step 4. Exact field names for the inline keyboard can shift between n8n versions — check the Telegram node's own UI if this doesn't match.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "update",
        "documentId": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "REPLACE_WITH_SHEET_ID"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "Content Calendar"
        },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "matchingColumns": [
            "row_number"
          ],
          "value": {
            "row_number": "={{ $('Find items due for review').item.json.row_number }}",
            "status": "Awaiting Approval",
            "telegram_message_id": "={{ $json.message_id }}"
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "update2",
      "name": "Mark Awaiting Approval",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1060,
        430
      ],
      "notes": "So this row is not asked about twice tomorrow, and workflow 3 can find it again by message id.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "updates": [
          "callback_query"
        ]
      },
      "id": "tgtrig3",
      "name": "Approval button tapped",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegramTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        840,
        660
      ],
      "notes": "Fires the instant you tap Approve or Reject on the Telegram message from workflow 2.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "name": "decision",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.callback_query.data.split('|')[0] }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "row_number",
              "type": "number",
              "value": "={{ Number($json.callback_query.data.split('|')[1]) }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "set3",
      "name": "Read the tap",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1060,
        660
      ],
      "notes": "Splits the callback_data 'approve|7' or 'reject|7' back into a decision and a row.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.decision }}",
              "rightValue": "approve",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "if3rep",
      "name": "Approved?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1280,
        660
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "update",
        "documentId": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "REPLACE_WITH_SHEET_ID"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "Content Calendar"
        },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "matchingColumns": [
            "row_number"
          ],
          "value": {
            "row_number": "={{ $json.row_number }}",
            "status": "Approved"
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "upd3a",
      "name": "Mark Approved",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        840,
        890
      ],
      "notes": "Workflow 4 picks this up at the row's scheduled_datetime and publishes it.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "update",
        "documentId": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "REPLACE_WITH_SHEET_ID"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "Content Calendar"
        },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "matchingColumns": [
            "row_number"
          ],
          "value": {
            "row_number": "={{ $json.row_number }}",
            "status": "Needs edit"
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "upd3b",
      "name": "Send back for editing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1060,
        890
      ],
      "notes": "Rejected items go back to 'Needs edit' — the next time you ping Claude to process pending rows, this one gets another auto-edit pass.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "callback",
        "operation": "answerQuery",
        "queryId": "={{ $('Approval button tapped').item.json.callback_query.id }}",
        "text": "Got it."
      },
      "id": "ack3",
      "name": "Acknowledge the tap",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1280,
        890
      ],
      "notes": "Stops Telegram showing a spinner on the button forever.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "minutes",
              "minutesInterval": 15
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "cron4",
      "name": "Every 15 minutes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1820,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "How close to the scheduled minute a video actually goes live depends on this interval.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "readRows",
        "documentId": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "REPLACE_WITH_SHEET_ID"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "Content Calendar"
        },
        "filtersUI": {
          "values": [
            {
              "lookupColumn": "status",
              "lookupValue": "Approved"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "read4",
      "name": "Find items due now",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2040,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "Approved rows only. A second check below drops anything not due yet.",
